n) Olympic team. The remaining 15 teams played in two round-robin pools, with the past two champions - India and Pakistan - emerging as the number one teams. India, however, had to allow two draws against Germany and Spain, while Pakistan won all six matches. Both squads met each other in the decider for the third time in a row. The match was played at a blistering pace, but remained goalless for a long time. Play had to be suspended briefly after a quarrel between some of the players. A penalty corner by India’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/19289"} "Prithipal Singh"] " was illegally stopped by fullback " [:a {:href "/athletes/19977"} "Munir Ahmed Dar"] ", which resulted in a penalty shot. " [:a {:href "/athletes/19208"} "Mohinder Lal"] " converted it, clinching the match for India."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button433315", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button433315').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Games Played", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "GP"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Goals"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {:class "accordion-toggle", :data-toggle "collapse", :data-target ".team-members-515978"} [:div {:class "glyphicon glyphicon-plus"}]] [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "India"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/IND"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/IND.png"}] "IND"]] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class " accordion-body team-members-515978 collapse", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:class "bib"} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/19211"} "Shankar Lax